      *================================================================*
      * ACCTMNT: ACCOUNT MAINTENANCE                                   *
      *                                                                *
      * APPLIES THE BRANCHES' MAINTENANCE REQUESTS TO THE MASTER AT    *
      * THE END OF THE DAY: OPENS ACCOUNTS, CLOSES THEM, FREEZES AND   *
      * UNFREEZES THEM, AND CHANGES OVERDRAFT LIMITS. THE REQUESTS     *
      * COME IN ACCOUNT NUMBER ORDER AND ARE MATCHED AGAINST THE       *
      * MASTER: EACH ACCOUNT IS HELD WHILE ITS REQUESTS APPLY, THEN    *
      * WRITTEN TO THE NEW MASTER. A REQUEST THAT CANNOT APPLY GOES TO *
      * THE REJECTS WITH ITS REASON.                                   *
      *                                                                *
      * RULES: AN OPENING NEEDS AN ACCOUNT NUMBER NOT YET USED; ANY    *
      * OTHER REQUEST AN ACCOUNT THAT EXISTS AND IS NOT CLOSED. ONLY   *
      * AN EMPTY ACCOUNT CLOSES. ONLY AN OPEN ACCOUNT FREEZES, ONLY A  *
      * FROZEN ONE UNFREEZES. ONLY CURRENT ACCOUNTS HAVE OVERDRAFTS.   *
      * MAINTENANCE NEVER MOVES MONEY: THE NEW MASTER MUST HOLD THE    *
      * SAME BALANCES AS THE OLD.                                      *
      *                                                                *
      * RETURN CODES: 0 ALL APPLIED, 4 SOME REJECTED,                  *
      *               16 INPUT OUT OF ORDER, OUT OF BALANCE OR I/O.    *
      *                                                                *
      * MODIFICATION HISTORY                                           *
      * DATE       BY  CHANGE                                          *
      * 1988-05-09 JA  CR-0031 ORIGINAL VERSION.                       *
      * 1994-11-14 PK  CR-0201 OVERDRAFT LIMIT CHANGES.                *
      * 1999-01-11 SL  Y2K: 8-DIGIT OPEN DATES.                        *
      *================================================================*
       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID. ACCTMNT.
       AUTHOR. J. ARKWRIGHT, BATCH SYSTEMS.
       INSTALLATION. FIRST BANK OF PANGAEA, DATA CENTER.
       DATE-WRITTEN. 1988-05-09.

       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
       INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
       FILE-CONTROL.
           SELECT CONTROL-FILE ASSIGN TO BANKCTL
               ORGANIZATION IS SEQUENTIAL
               FILE STATUS IS WS-CONTROL-STATUS.
           SELECT ACCT-IN      ASSIGN TO ACCTIN
               ORGANIZATION IS SEQUENTIAL
               FILE STATUS IS WS-ACCT-IN-STATUS.
           SELECT MAINT-IN     ASSIGN TO MAINTIN
               ORGANIZATION IS SEQUENTIAL
               FILE STATUS IS WS-MAINT-IN-STATUS.
           SELECT ACCT-OUT     ASSIGN TO ACCTOUT
               ORGANIZATION IS SEQUENTIAL
               FILE STATUS IS WS-ACCT-OUT-STATUS.
           SELECT REJECT-OUT   ASSIGN TO REJECTS
               ORGANIZATION IS SEQUENTIAL
               FILE STATUS IS WS-REJECT-STATUS.
           SELECT REPORT-OUT   ASSIGN TO MNTRPT
               ORGANIZATION IS LINE SEQUENTIAL
               FILE STATUS IS WS-REPORT-STATUS.

       DATA DIVISION.
       FILE SECTION.
       FD  CONTROL-FILE.
           COPY BANKCTL.
       FD  ACCT-IN.
       01  ACCT-IN-RECORD.
           05  AI-ACCT-NO              PIC X(10).
           05  FILLER                  PIC X(90).
       FD  MAINT-IN.
           COPY MAINTREC.
       FD  ACCT-OUT.
       01  ACCT-OUT-RECORD             PIC X(100).
       FD  REJECT-OUT.
       01  REJECT-OUT-RECORD           PIC X(100).
       FD  REPORT-OUT.
       01  REPORT-LINE                 PIC X(80).

       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
       01  WS-FILE-STATUSES.
           05  WS-CONTROL-STATUS       PIC XX.
           05  WS-ACCT-IN-STATUS       PIC XX.
           05  WS-MAINT-IN-STATUS      PIC XX.
           05  WS-ACCT-OUT-STATUS      PIC XX.
           05  WS-REJECT-STATUS        PIC XX.
           05  WS-REPORT-STATUS        PIC XX.

       01  WS-BUSINESS-DATE            PIC 9(8).
       01  WS-ABORT-MESSAGE            PIC X(40).

      * MATCH KEYS: HIGH-VALUES ONCE A FILE IS AT ITS END. THE ACTIVE
      * KEY IS THE LOWER OF THE TWO: THE ACCOUNT BEING WORKED ON.
       01  WS-MASTER-KEY               PIC X(10).
       01  WS-REQUEST-KEY              PIC X(10).
       01  WS-ACTIVE-KEY               PIC X(10).
       01  WS-PREV-MASTER-KEY          PIC X(10)      VALUE LOW-VALUES.
       01  WS-REQUEST-ORDER-KEY.
           05  WS-ROK-ACCT-NO          PIC X(10).
           05  WS-ROK-REQUEST-ID       PIC X(10).
       01  WS-PREV-REQUEST-ORDER-KEY   PIC X(20)      VALUE LOW-VALUES.

      * THE ACCOUNT HELD WHILE ITS REQUESTS APPLY.
       01  WS-HELD-SW                  PIC X.
           88  ACCOUNT-HELD            VALUE 'Y'.
           88  NOTHING-HELD            VALUE 'N'.
           COPY ACCTMAST.

           COPY REJREC.

       01  WS-TOTALS.
           05  WS-MASTERS-READ         PIC 9(8)       VALUE 0.
           05  WS-MASTERS-WRITTEN      PIC 9(8)       VALUE 0.
           05  WS-REQUEST-COUNT        PIC 9(8)       VALUE 0.
           05  WS-OPENED-COUNT         PIC 9(8)       VALUE 0.
           05  WS-CLOSED-COUNT         PIC 9(8)       VALUE 0.
           05  WS-FROZEN-COUNT         PIC 9(8)       VALUE 0.
           05  WS-UNFROZEN-COUNT       PIC 9(8)       VALUE 0.
           05  WS-LIMIT-COUNT          PIC 9(8)       VALUE 0.
           05  WS-REJECT-COUNT         PIC 9(8)       VALUE 0.
           05  WS-BALANCES-IN          PIC S9(13)V99  VALUE 0.
           05  WS-BALANCES-OUT         PIC S9(13)V99  VALUE 0.

       01  WS-REPORT-COUNT-LINE.
           05  WS-RC-LABEL             PIC X(30).
           05  WS-RC-VALUE             PIC ZZ,ZZZ,ZZ9.
           05  FILLER                  PIC X(40)      VALUE SPACES.
       01  WS-REPORT-AMOUNT-LINE.
           05  WS-RA-LABEL             PIC X(30).
           05  WS-RA-VALUE             PIC Z,ZZZ,ZZZ,ZZZ,ZZ9.99-.
           05  FILLER                  PIC X(29)      VALUE SPACES.

       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
      * MATCH UNTIL BOTH FILES END, THEN RECONCILE AND REPORT.
       0000-MAIN.
           PERFORM 1000-INITIALIZE
           PERFORM 2000-NEXT-ACCOUNT THRU 2999-EXIT
               UNTIL WS-MASTER-KEY = HIGH-VALUES
                 AND WS-REQUEST-KEY = HIGH-VALUES
           IF WS-BALANCES-OUT NOT = WS-BALANCES-IN
               MOVE 'NEW MASTER OUT OF BALANCE' TO WS-ABORT-MESSAGE
               PERFORM 9900-ABORT.
           PERFORM 8000-WRITE-REPORT
           PERFORM 9000-CLOSE-FILES
           IF WS-REJECT-COUNT > 0
               MOVE 4 TO RETURN-CODE
           ELSE
               MOVE 0 TO RETURN-CODE.
           STOP RUN.

      * OPEN THE FILES AND READ THE FIRST RECORD OF EACH.
       1000-INITIALIZE.
           OPEN INPUT  CONTROL-FILE ACCT-IN MAINT-IN
                OUTPUT ACCT-OUT REJECT-OUT REPORT-OUT
           IF WS-FILE-STATUSES NOT = ALL '0'
               DISPLAY 'ACCTMNT: CANNOT OPEN FILES ' WS-FILE-STATUSES
               MOVE 16 TO RETURN-CODE
               STOP RUN.
           READ CONTROL-FILE
               AT END
                   MOVE 'NO BANK CONTROL RECORD' TO WS-ABORT-MESSAGE
                   PERFORM 9900-ABORT.
           MOVE BC-BUSINESS-DATE TO WS-BUSINESS-DATE
           MOVE SPACES TO REJECT-RECORD
           PERFORM 1200-READ-MASTER THRU 1200-EXIT
           PERFORM 1300-READ-REQUEST THRU 1300-EXIT.

      * READ THE NEXT OLD MASTER RECORD, CHECKING ACCOUNT ORDER.
       1200-READ-MASTER.
           READ ACCT-IN
               AT END
                   MOVE HIGH-VALUES TO WS-MASTER-KEY
                   GO TO 1200-EXIT.
           MOVE AI-ACCT-NO TO WS-MASTER-KEY
           IF WS-MASTER-KEY NOT > WS-PREV-MASTER-KEY
               MOVE 'MASTER NOT IN ACCOUNT ORDER' TO WS-ABORT-MESSAGE
               PERFORM 9900-ABORT.
           MOVE WS-MASTER-KEY TO WS-PREV-MASTER-KEY
           ADD 1 TO WS-MASTERS-READ.
       1200-EXIT.
           EXIT.

      * READ THE NEXT REQUEST, CHECKING ITS ORDER.
       1300-READ-REQUEST.
           READ MAINT-IN
               AT END
                   MOVE HIGH-VALUES TO WS-REQUEST-KEY
                   GO TO 1300-EXIT.
           MOVE MR-ACCT-NO TO WS-REQUEST-KEY WS-ROK-ACCT-NO
           MOVE MR-REQUEST-ID TO WS-ROK-REQUEST-ID
           IF WS-REQUEST-ORDER-KEY NOT > WS-PREV-REQUEST-ORDER-KEY
               MOVE 'REQUESTS NOT IN ACCOUNT ORDER' TO WS-ABORT-MESSAGE
               PERFORM 9900-ABORT.
           MOVE WS-REQUEST-ORDER-KEY TO WS-PREV-REQUEST-ORDER-KEY
           ADD 1 TO WS-REQUEST-COUNT.
       1300-EXIT.
           EXIT.

      * TAKE THE LOWER KEY AS THE ACTIVE ACCOUNT, AND HOLD IT IF THE
      * MASTER HAS IT. AN ACCOUNT ONLY THE REQUESTS NAME IS NOT HELD
      * UNTIL AN OPENING MAKES IT.
       2000-NEXT-ACCOUNT.
           MOVE WS-MASTER-KEY TO WS-ACTIVE-KEY
           IF WS-REQUEST-KEY < WS-MASTER-KEY
               MOVE WS-REQUEST-KEY TO WS-ACTIVE-KEY.
           SET NOTHING-HELD TO TRUE
           IF WS-MASTER-KEY = WS-ACTIVE-KEY
               MOVE ACCT-IN-RECORD TO ACCT-MASTER-RECORD
               ADD AM-BALANCE TO WS-BALANCES-IN
               SET ACCOUNT-HELD TO TRUE
               PERFORM 1200-READ-MASTER THRU 1200-EXIT.

      * APPLY THE ACTIVE ACCOUNT'S REQUESTS, ONE AFTER THE OTHER.
       2100-APPLY-REQUESTS.
           IF WS-REQUEST-KEY NOT = WS-ACTIVE-KEY
               GO TO 2800-WRITE-HELD.
           PERFORM 2200-APPLY-REQUEST THRU 2299-EXIT
           PERFORM 1300-READ-REQUEST THRU 1300-EXIT
           GO TO 2100-APPLY-REQUESTS.

      * APPLY ONE REQUEST BY ITS TYPE.
       2200-APPLY-REQUEST.
           IF MR-OPEN
               GO TO 2210-OPEN.
           IF NOTHING-HELD
               SET RJ-NO-ACCOUNT TO TRUE
               GO TO 2290-REJECT.
           IF AM-CLOSED
               SET RJ-CLOSED TO TRUE
               GO TO 2290-REJECT.
           IF MR-CLOSE
               GO TO 2220-CLOSE.
           IF MR-FREEZE
               GO TO 2230-FREEZE.
           IF MR-UNFREEZE
               GO TO 2240-UNFREEZE.
           IF MR-LIMIT
               GO TO 2250-LIMIT.
           SET RJ-BAD-TYPE TO TRUE
           GO TO 2290-REJECT.

      * OPEN A NEW ACCOUNT, EMPTY, FROM TODAY.
       2210-OPEN.
           IF ACCOUNT-HELD
               SET RJ-EXISTS TO TRUE
               GO TO 2290-REJECT.
           MOVE SPACES TO ACCT-MASTER-RECORD
           MOVE MR-ACCT-NO TO AM-ACCT-NO
           MOVE MR-CUST-NO TO AM-CUST-NO
           MOVE MR-SHORT-NAME TO AM-SHORT-NAME
           MOVE MR-ACCT-TYPE TO AM-ACCT-TYPE
           SET AM-OPEN TO TRUE
           MOVE WS-BUSINESS-DATE TO AM-OPEN-DATE AM-LAST-ACTIVITY-DATE
           MOVE 0 TO AM-BALANCE
           MOVE MR-OVERDRAFT-LIMIT TO AM-OVERDRAFT-LIMIT
           IF AM-SAVINGS
               MOVE 0 TO AM-OVERDRAFT-LIMIT.
           SET ACCOUNT-HELD TO TRUE
           ADD 1 TO WS-OPENED-COUNT
           GO TO 2299-EXIT.

      * CLOSE AN ACCOUNT, IF IT IS EMPTY.
       2220-CLOSE.
           IF AM-BALANCE NOT = 0
               SET RJ-HAS-BALANCE TO TRUE
               GO TO 2290-REJECT.
           SET AM-CLOSED TO TRUE
           MOVE 0 TO AM-OVERDRAFT-LIMIT
           ADD 1 TO WS-CLOSED-COUNT
           GO TO 2299-EXIT.

      * FREEZE AN OPEN ACCOUNT.
       2230-FREEZE.
           IF NOT AM-OPEN
               SET RJ-BAD-STATUS TO TRUE
               GO TO 2290-REJECT.
           SET AM-FROZEN TO TRUE
           ADD 1 TO WS-FROZEN-COUNT
           GO TO 2299-EXIT.

      * UNFREEZE A FROZEN ACCOUNT.
       2240-UNFREEZE.
           IF NOT AM-FROZEN
               SET RJ-BAD-STATUS TO TRUE
               GO TO 2290-REJECT.
           SET AM-OPEN TO TRUE
           ADD 1 TO WS-UNFROZEN-COUNT
           GO TO 2299-EXIT.

      * CHANGE A CURRENT ACCOUNT'S OVERDRAFT LIMIT.
       2250-LIMIT.
           IF NOT AM-CURRENT
               SET RJ-BAD-TYPE TO TRUE
               GO TO 2290-REJECT.
           MOVE MR-OVERDRAFT-LIMIT TO AM-OVERDRAFT-LIMIT
           ADD 1 TO WS-LIMIT-COUNT
           GO TO 2299-EXIT.

      * WRITE THE REQUEST TO THE REJECTS WITH ITS REASON.
       2290-REJECT.
           MOVE 'ACCTMNT' TO RJ-PROGRAM
           MOVE MAINT-REQUEST TO RJ-TRAN
           WRITE REJECT-OUT-RECORD FROM REJECT-RECORD
           ADD 1 TO WS-REJECT-COUNT.
       2299-EXIT.
           EXIT.

      * WRITE THE HELD ACCOUNT, ITS REQUESTS APPLIED, TO THE NEW MASTER.
       2800-WRITE-HELD.
           IF ACCOUNT-HELD
               WRITE ACCT-OUT-RECORD FROM ACCT-MASTER-RECORD
               ADD 1 TO WS-MASTERS-WRITTEN
               ADD AM-BALANCE TO WS-BALANCES-OUT.
       2999-EXIT.
           EXIT.

      * WRITE THE MAINTENANCE REPORT.
       8000-WRITE-REPORT.
           MOVE SPACES TO REPORT-LINE
           STRING 'ACCTMNT  ACCOUNT MAINTENANCE     BUSINESS DATE '
                  WS-BUSINESS-DATE
               DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO REPORT-LINE
           WRITE REPORT-LINE
           MOVE SPACES TO REPORT-LINE
           WRITE REPORT-LINE
           MOVE 'ACCOUNTS READ' TO WS-RC-LABEL
           MOVE WS-MASTERS-READ TO WS-RC-VALUE
           WRITE REPORT-LINE FROM WS-REPORT-COUNT-LINE
           MOVE 'ACCOUNTS WRITTEN' TO WS-RC-LABEL
           MOVE WS-MASTERS-WRITTEN TO WS-RC-VALUE
           WRITE REPORT-LINE FROM WS-REPORT-COUNT-LINE
           MOVE 'REQUESTS READ' TO WS-RC-LABEL
           MOVE WS-REQUEST-COUNT TO WS-RC-VALUE
           WRITE REPORT-LINE FROM WS-REPORT-COUNT-LINE
           MOVE 'ACCOUNTS OPENED' TO WS-RC-LABEL
           MOVE WS-OPENED-COUNT TO WS-RC-VALUE
           WRITE REPORT-LINE FROM WS-REPORT-COUNT-LINE
           MOVE 'ACCOUNTS CLOSED' TO WS-RC-LABEL
           MOVE WS-CLOSED-COUNT TO WS-RC-VALUE
           WRITE REPORT-LINE FROM WS-REPORT-COUNT-LINE
           MOVE 'ACCOUNTS FROZEN' TO WS-RC-LABEL
           MOVE WS-FROZEN-COUNT TO WS-RC-VALUE
           WRITE REPORT-LINE FROM WS-REPORT-COUNT-LINE
           MOVE 'ACCOUNTS UNFROZEN' TO WS-RC-LABEL
           MOVE WS-UNFROZEN-COUNT TO WS-RC-VALUE
           WRITE REPORT-LINE FROM WS-REPORT-COUNT-LINE
           MOVE 'OVERDRAFT LIMITS CHANGED' TO WS-RC-LABEL
           MOVE WS-LIMIT-COUNT TO WS-RC-VALUE
           WRITE REPORT-LINE FROM WS-REPORT-COUNT-LINE
           MOVE 'REQUESTS REJECTED' TO WS-RC-LABEL
           MOVE WS-REJECT-COUNT TO WS-RC-VALUE
           WRITE REPORT-LINE FROM WS-REPORT-COUNT-LINE
           MOVE SPACES TO REPORT-LINE
           WRITE REPORT-LINE
           MOVE 'BALANCES' TO WS-RA-LABEL
           MOVE WS-BALANCES-OUT TO WS-RA-VALUE
           WRITE REPORT-LINE FROM WS-REPORT-AMOUNT-LINE
           MOVE SPACES TO REPORT-LINE
           WRITE REPORT-LINE
           MOVE 'NEW MASTER IN BALANCE' TO REPORT-LINE
           WRITE REPORT-LINE.

      * CLOSE ALL FILES.
       9000-CLOSE-FILES.
           CLOSE CONTROL-FILE ACCT-IN MAINT-IN ACCT-OUT
                 REJECT-OUT REPORT-OUT.

      * STOP THE RUN WITH RETURN CODE 16, SAYING WHY.
       9900-ABORT.
           DISPLAY 'ACCTMNT: ' WS-ABORT-MESSAGE
           PERFORM 9000-CLOSE-FILES
           MOVE 16 TO RETURN-CODE
           STOP RUN.
